Yeah, once we're done, I'm

1306
01:38:35,054 --> 01:38:36,219
I'm gonna die.

1307
01:38:38,456 --> 01:38:40,095
Why didn't you tell me?

1308
01:38:40,868 --> 01:38:42,738
It slipped my mind.

1309
01:38:42,740 --> 01:38:45,337
No.
Grace say Grace go home.

1310
01:38:45,338 --> 01:38:46,912
Look.

1311
01:38:46,913 --> 01:38:49,818
Listen. Listen. Listen.
- No. No.

1312
01:38:50,722 --> 01:38:52,615
I got to meet you.

1313
01:38:52,616 --> 01:38:55,060
I got to do
all this amazing stuff.

1314
01:38:55,061 --> 01:38:57,459
I'm good.
I've made peace with it.

1315
01:38:58,196 --> 01:39:00,433
What mean?
What mean "make peace"?

1316
01:39:00,434 --> 01:39:01,974
It means

1317
01:39:02,680 --> 01:39:05,146
I know I'm not going home

1318
01:39:05,147 --> 01:39:06,643
I know why

1319
01:39:06,644 --> 01:39:08,580
and it's okay.

1320
01:39:11,765 --> 01:39:13,734
Thumbs up?
- No.

1321
01:39:13,735 --> 01:39:15,429
Tiny thumbs up?
- No.

1322
01:39:16,367 --> 01:39:18,975
We got stars to save. Okay?

1323
01:39:23,789 --> 01:39:25,923
Grace?
- Yeah.

1324
01:39:26,651 --> 01:39:28,224
You are

1325
01:39:31,529 --> 01:39:32,905
Need word.

1326
01:39:32,906 --> 01:39:34,810
W-W-What word do you need?

1327
01:39:34,811 --> 01:39:37,045
To risk self to help another.

1328
01:39:37,046 --> 01:39:38,211
Uh, dumb.

1329
01:39:39,017 --> 01:39:40,512
Grace?

1330
01:40:06,104 --> 01:40:08,271
How much Astrophage
you need, question?

1331
01:40:09,242 --> 01:40:11,343
Two million kilograms.

1332
01:40:15,893 --> 01:40:17,553
I can give.

1333
01:40:20,837 --> 01:40:23,808
I go home six years slower.

1334
01:40:25,880 --> 01:40:27,441
That's too much.

1335
01:40:28,478 --> 01:40:30,150
Rocky watch crew die.

1336
01:40:30,747 --> 01:40:32,253
Could not fix.

1337
01:40:33,224 --> 01:40:35,061
Grace say Grace will die.

1338
01:40:35,867 --> 01:40:37,362
Rocky fix.

1339
01:40:53,462 --> 01:40:55,233
Grace go home.

1340
01:41:06,422 --> 01:41:07,719
Okay.

1341
01:41:30,173 --> 01:41:33,244
I thought
you made peace, question?

1342
01:41:33,245 --> 01:41:36,249
I didn't mean
any of that.

1343
01:41:37,220 --> 01:41:39,123
That's just something you say.

1344
01:41:46,370 --> 01:41:47,700
Thank you.

1345
01:41:56,225 --> 01:41:57,390
Get over here.

1346
01:41:59,892 --> 01:42:02,864
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
What? What's happening?

1347
01:42:02,865 --> 01:42:05,275
A hug.
- Oh! Hmm.

1348
01:42:05,276 --> 01:42:09,250
It's usually not something
one does by themselves.

1349
01:42:09,251 --> 01:42:10,913
Oh. Wait, I do the same?

1350
01:42:10,914 --> 01:42:12,585
Would you just get in here?

1351
01:42:20,802 --> 01:42:23,245
How do you know
when the hug is done?

1352
01:42:23,246 --> 01:42:25,314
You just feel it.
- Oh.

1353
01:42:26,714 --> 01:42:28,288
Are you feeling it now?

1354
01:42:28,289 --> 01:42:29,389
Nope.

1355
01:42:29,390 --> 01:42:30,853
Oh. Oh, okay. Yeah.

1356
01:42:36,173 --> 01:42:38,473
<i>We ran the sampler
simulation again this morning.</i>

1357
01:42:38,474 --> 01:42:40,742
Shapiro and DuBois
nailed it again.

1358
01:42:40,743 --> 01:42:42,612
Okay. What about the others?

1359
01:42:43,319 --> 01:42:44,683
They'll be ready.

1360
01:42:44,684 --> 01:42:46,015
I expect so.

1361
01:42:46,688 --> 01:42:48,195
They have a great teacher.

1362
01:42:51,731 --> 01:42:53,096
Can you
take a compliment please?

1363
01:42:53,097 --> 01:42:54,505
No.

1364
01:42:54,506 --> 01:42:56,212
It's an order. Okay?

1365
01:42:56,213 --> 01:42:59,580
Okay. If it's an order,
I'll take it. Thank you.

1366
01:43:00,254 --> 01:43:02,047
Good.

1367
01:43:04,328 --> 01:43:05,725
What do you think?

1368
01:43:05,726 --> 01:43:08,598
It's pretty impressive.

1369
01:43:09,470 --> 01:43:10,867
Yeah.
- You're

1370
01:43:12,311 --> 01:43:13,476
You're good.

1371
01:43:17,255 --> 01:43:19,356
- Three days, huh?

1372
01:43:21,021 --> 01:43:22,197
Yeah.

1373
01:43:23,696 --> 01:43:27,032
So, what are you gonna do
for the next 20 years?

1374
01:43:27,033 --> 01:43:28,099
You got a plan?

1375
01:44:20,745 --> 01:44:23,011
<i>Manual mode activated.</i>

1376
01:44:28,959 --> 01:44:30,025
Go.

1377
01:45:01,188 --> 01:45:02,464
That's not half bad!

1378
01:45:02,465 --> 01:45:03,862
Is full good.

1379
01:45:10,415 --> 01:45:11,879
Time go fishing, question?

1380
01:45:11,880 --> 01:45:13,518
It's now or never.

1381
01:45:25,743 --> 01:45:27,140
Three thousand meters.
- Three thousand.

1382
01:45:27,141 --> 01:45:28,449
Probe signal good.

1383
01:45:45,915 --> 01:45:47,620
Now comes the fun part.

1384
01:45:47,621 --> 01:45:48,887
Grace go out on hull
to retrieve collector?

1385
01:45:48,888 --> 01:45:49,955
No fun at all.

1386
01:45:49,956 --> 01:45:51,254
It's a joke.

1387
01:45:51,255 --> 01:45:53,598
Oh, humor. Confusing.

1388
01:46:00,339 --> 01:46:02,012
You gotta be kidding me.

1389
01:46:02,013 --> 01:46:03,212
What problem, question?

1390
01:46:03,213 --> 01:46:05,315
It's fine. It's just

1391
01:46:05,316 --> 01:46:08,056
the sky is slightly on fire.

1392
01:46:11,196 --> 01:46:12,361
Words of encouragement.

1393
01:46:13,231 --> 01:46:15,268
You can't just say
"words of encouragement."

1394
01:46:16,305 --> 01:46:18,308
<i>Words of great encouragement.</i>

1395
01:46:18,309 --> 01:46:19,584
<i>Nope.</i>

1396
01:46:41,421 --> 01:46:43,291
<i>Did you feel that?</i>
- Yes.

1397
01:46:44,130 --> 01:46:46,672
I'm not worried.
Are you worried?

1398
01:46:46,673 --> 01:46:47,840
Yes.

1399
01:46:47,841 --> 01:46:48,973
Great.

1400
01:47:03,102 --> 01:47:05,676
Collector is closed.
Move winch into position.

1401
01:47:09,477 --> 01:47:10,984
- Whoa!

1402
01:47:17,625 --> 01:47:19,231
<i>How long
is this supposed to take?</i>

1403
01:47:20,973 --> 01:47:22,436
<i>Collector should be here soon.</i>

1404
01:47:22,437 --> 01:47:24,275
Yeah. It's here.

1405
01:47:24,276 --> 01:47:25,441
Amaze, amaze, amaze!

1406
01:47:30,728 --> 01:47:32,192
Careful. Collector important.

1407
01:47:32,193 --> 01:47:33,931
Yup.

1408
01:47:36,741 --> 01:47:38,876
<i>Altitude warning.</i>

1409
01:47:38,877 --> 01:47:39,910
Oh, hurry, hurry.

1410
01:47:56,208 --> 01:47:57,538
Hurry, hurry.

1411
01:48:08,298 --> 01:48:09,838
Grace?

1412
01:48:12,813 --> 01:48:13,945
Grace, status update.

1413
01:48:15,279 --> 01:48:16,819
Status update.

1414
01:48:17,448 --> 01:48:18,613
<i>Grace?</i>

1415
01:48:20,355 --> 01:48:21,797
<i>Grace is safe, question?</i>

1416
01:48:21,798 --> 01:48:24,032
I'm okay.

1417
01:48:24,033 --> 01:48:25,529
Good, good, good.

1418
01:48:25,530 --> 01:48:27,334
Come inside
with predator collector now.

1419
01:48:29,241 --> 01:48:31,079
Uh

1420
01:48:31,080 --> 01:48:33,214
<i>Why not moving, question?</i>

1421
01:48:34,890 --> 01:48:37,652
<i>Warning!
Exterior temperature elevated.</i>

1422
01:48:37,653 --> 01:48:39,556
Must move now. Go, go.

1423
01:48:48,378 --> 01:48:50,546
No, Grace.
Bad idea. Come inside.

1424
01:48:50,547 --> 01:48:52,385
I'll be there in a minute.

1425
01:48:52,386 --> 01:48:54,256
<i>No, no, no,
no, no. Grace will die.</i>

1426
01:48:55,026 --> 01:48:56,867
Can repeat mission.
Can try again later.

1427
01:48:56,868 --> 01:48:58,529
I don't think
there is gonna be a later.

1428
01:48:58,530 --> 01:49:00,765
Abort, abort, abort.

1429
01:49:00,766 --> 01:49:03,505
<i>Grace will die.
No-No-No-No-No-No-No-No-No.</i>

1430
01:49:34,338 --> 01:49:35,911
Grace?
- I'm here!

1431
01:49:36,981 --> 01:49:38,411
Amaze, amaze, amaze!

1432
01:49:38,412 --> 01:49:40,184
- Grace okay, question?

1433
01:49:40,185 --> 01:49:42,056
Well, I'm not dead, so yes.

1434
01:49:42,057 --> 01:49:43,553
Good, good, good, good.

1435
01:49:43,554 --> 01:49:45,722
Where
is that noise coming from?

1436
01:49:45,723 --> 01:49:47,165
Noise is from all around.

1437
01:49:47,166 --> 01:49:49,896
It's loudest
at port side of bedroom.

1438
01:49:49,897 --> 01:49:53,374
The gravity's
tearing the ship apart.

1439
01:49:55,182 --> 01:49:56,612
We leave now, question?

1440
01:49:56,613 --> 01:49:59,122
We leave now, statement.

1441
01:50:10,146 --> 01:50:12,116
<i>Hull pressure warning.</i>

1442
01:50:12,117 --> 01:50:14,186
Hull bending
in big room below bedroom.

1443
01:50:14,187 --> 01:50:15,319
That's the fuel tanks.

1444
01:50:17,556 --> 01:50:19,824
Oh. Bad, bad, bad.
- Well, it's not great.

1445
01:50:19,825 --> 01:50:21,167
Bad, bad, bad.
- <i>Warning.</i>

1446
01:50:21,168 --> 01:50:23,434
Everybody, calm down.
Calm down!

1447
01:50:27,147 --> 01:50:28,610
Try and keep
yourself together, Mary.

1448
01:50:28,611 --> 01:50:30,119
Stop engine now?
- Not yet.

1449
01:50:30,120 --> 01:50:32,156
We need to get
into orbit or we'll crash!

1450
01:50:32,157 --> 01:50:34,953
I have an idea.
First, no crash.

1451
01:50:34,954 --> 01:50:37,166
Then, not explode. Deal?

1452
01:50:37,167 --> 01:50:38,332
Deal!

1453
01:50:40,404 --> 01:50:42,307
Hold on.

1454
01:50:43,906 --> 01:50:45,413
Now?

1455
01:50:45,414 --> 01:50:46,579
Wait.

1456
01:50:49,786 --> 01:50:51,028
Now? Now?

1457
01:50:52,296 --> 01:50:54,034
Now!

1458
01:51:05,289 --> 01:51:06,487
Did we do it?

1459
01:51:28,203 --> 01:51:29,600
Why ship moving, question?

1460
01:51:29,601 --> 01:51:30,998
There's a hole in it!

1461
01:51:32,442 --> 01:51:34,181
- <i>Hull breach.</i>

1462
01:51:34,182 --> 01:51:36,878
<i>Port side fuel compartments
11 and 12.</i>

1463
01:51:39,654 --> 01:51:42,086
Grace.
What happening, question?

1464
01:51:43,090 --> 01:51:45,730
The fuel
is migrating to Adrian!

1465
01:51:50,941 --> 01:51:53,043
Eject bad fuel bay, question?

1466
01:51:53,044 --> 01:51:55,014
Yeah.

1467
01:51:55,015 --> 01:51:58,492
<i>Jettison port fuel tank
compartment 12. Confirm.</i>

1468
01:52:07,644 --> 01:52:09,845
Rocky!

1469
01:52:20,736 --> 01:52:25,074
<i>Jettison port fuel tank
compartment 11. Confirm.</i>

1470
01:52:25,075 --> 01:52:27,715
Eject other fuel bay.

1471
01:55:42,976 --> 01:55:44,505
One nanogram of Astrophage

1472
01:55:44,506 --> 01:55:46,884
just isn't enough
to blow up a building.

1473
01:55:46,885 --> 01:55:48,822
The quartermaster gave him

1474
01:55:48,823 --> 01:55:50,187
one milligram by mistake.

1475
01:55:50,188 --> 01:55:51,927
That's a million times
the heat energy

1476
01:55:51,928 --> 01:55:53,655
that they're prepared for.

1477
01:55:53,656 --> 01:55:56,705
A measuring mistake
killed my entire science team?

1478
01:55:56,706 --> 01:55:59,303
It doesn't matter.
We have to launch.

1479
01:56:06,022 --> 01:56:08,796
If we miss the orbital window,
it'll set us back months.

1480
01:56:08,797 --> 01:56:10,359
Yeah,
but if no one's trained

1481
01:56:10,360 --> 01:56:12,066
to do the mission,
it won't matter.

1482
01:56:12,067 --> 01:56:13,662
Casualty projections
go up exponentially

1483
01:56:13,663 --> 01:56:14,742
if we delay.

1484
01:56:14,743 --> 01:56:16,041
We launch on schedule

1485
01:56:16,042 --> 01:56:17,175
with a replacement
science officer.

1486
01:56:17,176 --> 01:56:18,715
Okay, but

1487
01:56:20,512 --> 01:56:21,545
who?

1488
01:56:23,518 --> 01:56:25,862
I mean, that

1489
01:56:41,863 --> 01:56:43,128
I'm not an astronaut.

1490
01:56:43,129 --> 01:56:44,835
I don't need an astronaut.

1491
01:56:44,836 --> 01:56:47,400
I need an expert on Astrophage
who's mission-ready.

1492
01:56:47,401 --> 01:56:48,500
I'm not ready.

1493
01:56:49,370 --> 01:56:52,542
I don't have any training.

1494
01:56:52,543 --> 01:56:53,952
You'll pick it up.

1495
01:56:53,953 --> 01:56:55,316
I'm not an astronaut!

1496
01:56:55,986 --> 01:56:57,960
I put the "not" in astronaut.

1497
01:56:57,961 --> 01:56:59,655
I've never done anything--

1498
01:56:59,656 --> 01:57:01,792
I've never done a space wa--
I can't even moonwalk!

1499
01:57:01,793 --> 01:57:03,796
I haven't done
the whole pool thing.

1500
01:57:03,797 --> 01:57:05,800
No, no, no. This is just we do
for the picture,

1501
01:57:05,801 --> 01:57:07,011
for social media.

1502
01:57:07,012 --> 01:57:09,114
I'm not heroic in any way.

1503
01:57:09,115 --> 01:57:11,415
I get sick on an elevator.

1504
01:57:11,416 --> 01:57:13,860
Oh, perfect. There's
no elevator on the ship.

1505
01:57:13,861 --> 01:57:15,258
I cannot do this.

1506
01:57:15,259 --> 01:57:17,261
You're smart.
You'll figure it out.

1507
01:57:20,269 --> 01:57:23,208
This might be very hard
for you to understand,

1508
01:57:23,209 --> 01:57:24,882
but some people are failures.

1509
01:57:24,883 --> 01:57:26,709
Some people <i>don't</i> rise
to the challenge.

1510
01:57:26,710 --> 01:57:29,253
You've been present
for every major scientific

1511
01:57:29,254 --> 01:57:31,587
or strategic meeting
we've had on the mission.

1512
01:57:31,588 --> 01:57:33,856
You're missing out an
important part of the mission

1513
01:57:33,857 --> 01:57:35,794
which is the suicide part.

1514
01:57:35,795 --> 01:57:38,304
Grace, you'd be
in very cool company.

1515
01:57:38,305 --> 01:57:40,473
If you don't go,
you die anyway.

1516
01:57:40,474 --> 01:57:43,677
Yeah,
but I die in 30 years with--

1517
01:57:43,678 --> 01:57:44,921
"With the rest of us."

1518
01:57:46,288 --> 01:57:49,259
You have no immediate family.
You don't even have a dog.

1519
01:57:52,102 --> 01:57:54,005
So, just so I'm clear

1520
01:57:54,899 --> 01:57:57,077
you're asking me right now

1521
01:57:59,512 --> 01:58:00,612
to give up my life.

1522
01:58:00,613 --> 01:58:02,450
I am. We all are.

1523
01:58:06,857 --> 01:58:08,232
Can I think about this?

1524
01:58:08,233 --> 01:58:09,365
You have three hours.

1525
01:58:54,953 --> 01:58:57,032
<i>Eye movement detected.</i>

1526
01:58:58,465 --> 01:59:00,236
<i>Good morning, Dr. Grace.</i>

1527
02:00:19,022 --> 02:00:21,024
I'll watch you sleep, pal.

1528
02:00:28,172 --> 02:00:29,513
But, uh

1529
02:00:31,255 --> 02:00:32,784
you gotta wake up.

1530
02:01:07,624 --> 02:01:09,296
<i>I'm not sure what to do.</i>

1531
02:01:14,165 --> 02:01:16,167
<i>Done everything I can think of.</i>

1532
02:01:22,016 --> 02:01:23,654
<i>I made him a heat lamp.</i>

1533
02:01:46,361 --> 02:01:48,804
<i>And he left me
one last message.</i>

1534
02:03:30,944 --> 02:03:32,947
We have our predator.

1535
02:03:32,948 --> 02:03:35,821
Right now
I'm calling it "Taumoeba."

1536
02:03:35,822 --> 02:03:38,551
And I'm sure
that when you wake up,

1537
02:03:38,552 --> 02:03:42,295
you'll have a lot to say
about why that's a bad name

1538
02:03:42,296 --> 02:03:44,839
because it's just
an amoeba from Tau Ceti,

1539
02:03:44,840 --> 02:03:46,942
and we're putting "Tau"
in front of "amoeba."

1540
02:03:46,943 --> 02:03:49,882
But I would argue there's
an elegance to that.

1541
02:03:49,883 --> 02:03:51,049
A simplicity.

1542
02:03:51,050 --> 02:03:52,888
Let's not fight about it now.

1543
02:03:52,889 --> 02:03:55,618
We'll table it and we'll--

1544
02:03:55,619 --> 02:03:57,964
I did a test at different
atmospheric variables

1545
02:03:57,965 --> 02:04:01,168
and, fun fact, every time
I introduced nitrogen

1546
02:04:01,169 --> 02:04:02,875
it died.

1547
02:04:02,876 --> 02:04:04,438
And I know
what you're thinking,

1548
02:04:04,439 --> 02:04:06,442
"Well, that's terrible
because that's a problem

1549
02:04:06,443 --> 02:04:09,547
'cause we need it to survive
in the conditions of Venus."

1550
02:04:09,548 --> 02:04:11,221
Obviously, I had to figure out
how to breed

1551
02:04:11,222 --> 02:04:13,764
a new strain of
nitrogen-resistant Taumoeba.

1552
02:04:15,164 --> 02:04:16,870
And guess what I used?

1553
02:04:16,871 --> 02:04:20,535
The breeder tanks that we made
with your xenonite.

1554
02:04:21,715 --> 02:04:23,244
And you know what?

1555
02:04:24,755 --> 02:04:27,022
Now we're just
a couple of very cool dudes

1556
02:04:27,023 --> 02:04:30,766
with their very own strain of
nitrogen-resistant Taumoeba.

1557
02:04:30,767 --> 02:04:32,428
Really, all we have to do now

1558
02:04:32,429 --> 02:04:34,972
is breed enough
to survive the trip.

1559
02:04:34,973 --> 02:04:37,042
And you gotta wake up

1560
02:04:37,043 --> 02:04:38,341
because I don't know how to get

1561
02:04:38,342 --> 02:04:40,311
your half
of the Taumoeba to Erid.

1562
02:04:41,579 --> 02:04:42,855
